// A class cannot contain itself THROUGH ANOTHER CLASS either. Roadmap B40.
//
// `class A { b: B }` with `class B { a: A }` has no finite size: sizeof(A) includes sizeof(B),
// which includes sizeof(A). Stage-0 always refused it. Stage-1's check compared the field's type
// NAME against the class's own name — so it caught `class A { a: A }` and nothing one step
// further out, and it emitted 24,780 bytes of IR for a type whose size has no answer.
//
// This is the fixture that did not exist. The differential runs both compilers over the suite and
// reports every disagreement, and it can only disagree about a program somebody wrote.
//
// The fix needed a SECOND pass, and that is the part worth remembering: the declaration table is
// filled by the same loop that was doing the checking, so looking a class up during it answers
// "no such class" for every one of them. The direct check never noticed because it compares source
// text rather than looking anything up.
class A { b: B }
class B { a: A }

let x: Int = 1;
print(x);
